\title{tiltedTMLE: Targeted Maximum Likelihood Estimation for Tilted Average Treatment Effects}
\description{
Implements targeted maximum likelihood estimators (TMLE) for a broad
class of tilted average treatment effect (ATE) estimands, covering two
related but distinct tilting-function settings. Fang, He, and Dai,
"Targeted Learning for Externally Controlled Trials and Beyond" (AbbVie,
2026), treats the tilting function \code{h(x)} as a known, fixed weight
prespecified by the user, estimated with a single targeting step. Fang,
"Targeted Learning for Tilted Average Treatment Effects" (AbbVie, 2026),
instead treats \code{h(x)} as a known function of an unknown nuisance
function that must itself be estimated and iteratively targeted
alongside the outcome regression.
}
\section{Fixed/precomputed tilting functions}{

\code{\link[=estimate_tau_h_fixed]{estimate_tau_h_fixed()}} / \code{\link[=tmle_h]{tmle_h()}}: \code{h(x)} is either a fixed, precomputed
vector (e.g. \code{h(x) = 1} for the ATE), or a function evaluated once at
the fitted propensity score and never re-targeted (e.g. \verb{h(x) =} the
estimated propensity score itself for the ATT).
}

\section{Internally tilted estimands}{

\code{\link[=estimate_tau_h_internal_tilted]{estimate_tau_h_internal_tilted()}} / \code{\link[=tmle_tilted_h]{tmle_tilted_h()}}: ATE, ATT, ATC, ATO,
obtained by tilting the ATE by \code{h(x) = eta(g(x))}, a known function of
the treatment propensity score \code{g(x)}, within a single study population
(see \code{\link[=tilt_spec]{tilt_spec()}}). \code{g(x)} is iteratively targeted alongside the
outcome regression.
}

\section{Externally tilted estimands}{

\code{\link[=estimate_tau_h_external_tilted]{estimate_tau_h_external_tilted()}} / \code{\link[=tmle_external_tilted_h]{tmle_external_tilted_h()}}:
ATE-I, ATE-E, ATE-O, obtained by tilting by \code{h(x) = eta(s(x))}, a known
function of the selection propensity score \code{s(x)} between an internal
trial population and an external covariate-only population (see
